# What busybox's init does on the host: this file is laid over Alpine's own
# inittab, which starts OpenRC (not in the mini root filesystem) and puts no
# shell on a serial console. Each line is <tty>::<when>:<what>.
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t proc proc /proc
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t sysfs sysfs /sys
# Pseudo-terminals, which a shell over ssh runs on.
::sysinit:/bin/mkdir -p /dev/pts
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t devpts devpts /dev/pts
::sysinit:/bin/hostname socpuppet
# The network card, up from the start, for DHCP to ask on: Alpine has
# ifupdown bring it up, which the mini root does not carry.
::sysinit:/sbin/ip link set eth0 up
# A shell, and no login, on hvc0, the virtio console: Linux's console on the
# host, by the decision of 2026-10-18 (docs/history/decisions.md), and where
# the exit test of M20 waits for the prompt. The leading - makes it a login
# shell, which reads /etc/profile.
hvc0::respawn:-/bin/sh
# 🔌 An address by DHCP, where a cable to this machine's network is plugged
# in (sp.EthernetCable): udhcpc asks twice, a second apart, before the
# shell starts, and without an answer keeps asking in the background (-b).
# ⚠️ Before the shell, since udhcpc clears the card's addresses as it
# starts, and one typed at the shell would go. What it says goes nowhere:
# on the console it would come among what is typed there.
::sysinit:/sbin/udhcpc -i eth0 -b -t 2 -T 1 >/dev/null 2>&1
# The SSH server: dropbear, which makes its host key at the first
# connection (-R) and lets root in with no password (-B), as the console
# does: firmware/build.py clears root's (clear_roots_password). Only this
# machine reaches it, through the cable's port forwarded from 127.0.0.1.
::once:/usr/sbin/dropbear -R -B
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
